        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Tassel of silk cotton, possibly made in France or England, 1830-1860."@en , "Tassel consisting of a cord and a tassel body. The cord is made of red silk over cotton, and the multiple-shape body is of elaborately carved wood covered with red and white silk and red silk nets. From the body hangs a big skirt of cords of two thicknesses."@en ;
